Z||000000||merlin||08-03-2000||03:24 PM||||Hi, I have been unsuccessful at getting the correct fuel injector O-Rings for my 1987 GT.  On three occasions I was given the wrong part(s).  I explicitly ask for fuel injector o-rings not fuel rail o-rings, but I am continually given o-rings that look like fuel rail o-rings.  Now on my fourth attempt I order the o-rings from Carparts.com and after I placed the order I realized that the same part number (SK9) is associated with one item that's described as 'fuel injector o-rings' and another as 'fuel-rail' o-rings.  These are obviously different items...  Does anyone know what the deal is or what the correct manufacturer and part number is for fuel injector o-rings for a V6?  Thanks for any help.||||reg||8
Z||000001||AkursedX||08-03-2000||04:39 PM||||Well I'm looking in my parts catalog right now, and the o-ring that go in between the fuel rail and injector, and the o-ring that goes onto the tip of the injector are the same o-ring.  Unfortunately, I can't seem to find a part number.<BR>The only other o-rings that i see on here are o rings to the cold start injector, maybe that is what you're getting.  <BR>Hope I helped a little.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||mshill||08-03-2000||04:59 PM||||I got mine at autozone and they sell a complete kit.  The o-rings were all the same.<P>||||reg||1
